{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#def:canonical-neighborhood","title":"def:canonical-neighborhood","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions.md","line":1613,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions.tex#def:canonical-neighborhood","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:epsilon-neck]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#def:c-epsilon-cap]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#def:c-component]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#def:epsilon-round-component]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions.tex","label":"def:canonical-neighborhood","line":1831,"source":"\\begin{definition}[$(C,\\epsilon)$-canonical neighborhood]\\label{def:canonical-neighborhood}\n\\uses{def:epsilon-neck, def:c-epsilon-cap, def:c-component, def:epsilon-round-component}\n\nAn open neighborhood $U$ of $x$ in a Riemannian manifold is a\n\\emph{$(C,\\epsilon)$-canonical neighborhood} if it is one of:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item[(1)] an $\\epsilon$-neck centered at $x$;\n\\item[(2)] a $(C,\\epsilon)$-cap whose core contains $x$;\n\\item[(3)] a $C$-component;\n\\item[(4)] an $\\epsilon$-round component.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{definition}\n\n\\begin{definition}[Evolving and strong $\\epsilon$-neck; strong canonical neighborhood]","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(C,\\epsilon )$\">$(C,\\epsilon )$</span>-canonical neighborhood]<span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a63616e6f6e6963616c2d6e65696768626f